WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:16.000
Minimum hourly pay from April 2026: £12.71 (aged 21 or over), £10.85 (18 to 20), £8 (under 18 and apprentices). Announced for April 2027: £13.21 (21+), £11.27 (18 to 20) and £8.31 (16 to 17 and apprentices).

2
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:24.300
Before you start, the employer must check your right to work (for example, with a share code).

3
00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:38.000
If you work more than 6 hours a day, you are entitled to an unbroken 20-minute break, 11 hours' rest between working days and 24 hours a week.

4
00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:47.500
You must get a payslip no later than payday, showing your gross pay, net pay and deductions.

5
00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:54.700
Now do the lesson exercises. If you are unsure, watch this video again.
